MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
The letters before the comma say what a skip keeps: T keeps the text
between the delimiters and D keeps the delimiters themselves.
MCDEF WORD AS <REPLACED>
MCSKIP DT,' '
'WORD is quoted and kept'
MCSKIP T,( )
(WORD is bracketed and the brackets go)
MCSKIP DROPME
WORD DROPME WORD
With neither letter the whole construction disappears, delimiters
and text alike.
MCSKIP [ ]
before [WORD and everything here] after
